A dangling plus is a letter, and a nested quote reads it like an unnested one

```
> q
+

para
.
<blockquote><p>q
+</p></blockquote>
<p>para</p>
```

```
> q
+
.
<blockquote><p>q
+</p></blockquote>
```

```
- a
+

para
.
<ul>
  <li>a
+</li>
</ul>
<p>para</p>
```

```
x[^a]

[^a]: note
+

para
.
<p>x<a id="fnref1" href="#fn1" role="doc-noteref"><sup>1</sup></a></p>
<p>para</p>
<section role="doc-endnotes" aria-label="Footnotes">
  <hr>
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">
      <p>note
+<a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink" aria-label="Back to reference">↩</a></p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>
```

```
> > q
> +
> para
.
<blockquote>
  <blockquote>
    <p>q</p>
    <p>para</p>
  </blockquote>
</blockquote>
```

